WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.803
-After months of saying
he didn't want a war with Iran,

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.472
last night the president
threatened a war with Iran,

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:07.974
in order to protect
Saudi Arabia.

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:10.309
For more on this,
it's time for A Closer Look.

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:14.480
♪♪

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.349
So you know how
every night on this show,

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.917
we establish that
the Trump administration

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.919
is full of corrupt,
self-dealing con artists

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.221
who lie pathologically
about virtually everything,

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:23.823
even the dumbest things --
you know,

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.157
things like hurricane maps?

00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:27.994
Well, on Friday,
we got another example

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.996
of the Trump administration's
war on the truth,

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:32.432
when the vice president
told a weird story

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:35.334
about a Triple Crown winning
horse biting him.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.236
-Vice President
Mike Pence reveals

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:39.639
Triple Crown winner
American Pharoah

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.540
bit him on the arm.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.444
Pence told the story
during a policy retreat today

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:46.579
for House Republicans
in Baltimore.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.381
He says he was helping campaign

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:50.282
for Congressman Andy Barr
last year,

00:00:50.282 --> 00:00:53.052
when the two were invited
to see the prize-winning horse

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:54.453
in Lexington.

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:58.224
-Andy and I were standing there,
posing for all the cameras,

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:01.093
and American Pharoah bit me
so hard on the arm,

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:03.429
I almost collapsed.

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:06.031
-That's right. Mike Pence claims
American Pharoah bit him.

00:01:06.031 --> 00:01:09.035
This is the biggest political
scandal involving a horse

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:12.105
since Secretariat took a dump
on Richard Nixon's desk.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.506
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.275
And by the way,
when the news broke

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:16.743
that American Pharoah bit Pence,

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:19.044
he immediately rocketed
to the top of the polls

00:01:19.044 --> 00:01:21.915
in the Democratic primary.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.050
Now, for what it's worth...

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.486
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.321
For what it's worth,
I always assumed

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:31.057
the politician to most likely
tell a crazy horse story

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:33.025
was Joe Biden.

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:35.027
"I met Seabiscuit in 1938.

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:37.063
He looked that horse
right in the eyes.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:40.466
I shook his hoof, and I said,
'Best of luck out there, fella.'

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:41.700
Then they opened the gates,

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.337
and I beat that horse
in the Kentucky Derby."

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.439
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.641
I mean, it would
certainly be less crazy

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.476
than this insane answer
Biden gave

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:52.278
during the Democratic debate
on Thursday,

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.847
when asked about the legacy
of slavery in America.

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:57.083
First, he couldn't even
get through the question

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.318
without screwing up.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.386
-Mr. Vice President,
I want to come to you

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:03.589
and talk to you about inequality
in schools and race.

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:05.892
-[ Chuckles ]
-Alright, whoa.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:08.594
Right off the bat, I mean,
what's with the scoff there?

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:11.197
This is a debate. You have
to answer tough questions,

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.732
you know?
It's not the State of the Union

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.534
where you get to just
sit in the background

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.901
and do finger guns all night

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:18.670
like a Hollywood agent
at an Oscar party.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:20.072
"Leo, you're crushing it.

00:02:20.072 --> 00:02:22.041
Brad, I'm going to see you
at the Playboy Mansion later.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.243
Going to see you
in the grotto, Brad."

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:28.815
And then Biden's answer
only got worse from there.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.316
-What responsibility
do you think

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.617
that Americans need to take

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:34.987
to repair the legacy of slavery
in our country?

00:02:34.987 --> 00:02:36.856
-Well, they have
to deal with the --

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:40.093
Look, there's institutional
segregation in this country.

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:42.027
Look. Talk about education.

00:02:42.027 --> 00:02:44.864
I propose that what we take
is those very poor schools,

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.232
the Title I schools,

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.533
triple the amount
of money we spend

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:49.568
from $15 billion
to $45 billion a year.

00:02:49.568 --> 00:02:51.737
Number two, make sure
that we bring in

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:53.873
to help the stu-- the teachers

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.008
deal with the problem
that come from home,

00:02:56.008 --> 00:02:58.544
we bring social workers
into homes with parents

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:01.580
to help them deal with
how to raise their children.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:03.015
It's not that
they don't want to help.

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:05.518
They don't know
quite what to do.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.920
Play the radio.
Make sure the television --

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.257
Excuse me. Make sure you have
the record player on at night,

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:14.627
the phone --
Make sure the kids hear words.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.196
-What are you talking about?
What?

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:19.798
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.798 --> 00:03:22.602
Your solution to repair
the legacy of slavery

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:23.736
is for parents to make sure

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.638
they have the record player on
at night?

00:03:26.638 --> 00:03:29.008
"Hey, and I'll tell you
another thing. I don't like

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:33.312
these new steam-powered
locomotives they got out there.

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:34.613
Kids need exercise.

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:38.451
Whatever happened to the good,
old-fashioned hand car?"

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:40.319
Anyway, we're off-track here,

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:41.921
because, you know,
that's how things are now.

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:45.391
The important thing is,
a horse bit Mike Pence.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.492
Great!

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:49.696
Or so he said.

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:51.664
The story got laughs. That
should have been the end of it.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.499
Yet, as we have learned
with this administration

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:56.602
over and over and over again,
nothing, not even the smallest,

00:03:56.602 --> 00:04:00.706
most inconsequential
equine details can be trusted,

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:04.677
because now even the story
about getting bit by a horse

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:07.981
is being questioned
by the horse's manager,

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:10.950
who said, "If he gave someone
a nasty bite, I'd know it,"

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.819
adding that such behavior
would be unexpected

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:16.322
from a sweet horse.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:20.192
Well? Who you going
to believe --

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:24.396
The Vice President of the United
States or a horse manager?

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:25.998
Seriously. I'm asking.

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:29.368
I do not know who to believe
in this situation,

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:31.938
but I'm definitely not inclined
to side with these guys,

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:33.939
because they lie
about everything.

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:35.741
And you have to ask yourself,
if they're willing to lie

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:38.010
about something as dumb
as a weather forecast

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:40.813
or an interaction with a horse,
what else are they lying about?

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:43.382
For example, over the weekend,
Trump lashed out

00:04:43.382 --> 00:04:44.683
at media reports

00:04:44.683 --> 00:04:47.019
that he was willing
to meet with Iran's president

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:50.155
after he ripped up the Obama-era
nuclear deal with Iran.

00:04:50.155 --> 00:04:52.324
-The president tweeting,
"The Fake News is saying

00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:55.528
that I am willing to meet
with Iran, 'No Conditions.'

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:58.765
That is an incorrect statement
(as usual!)."

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.500
-Okay, first of all,
no one thought you'd meet

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.334
with no conditions,
because for one thing,

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:06.939
you definitely have several
diagnosable conditions.

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:10.476
Even if it was a meeting
with the president of France,

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:12.044
it would have conditions there,

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:15.147
you know, like narcissistic
personality disorder.

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:16.616
Second, why does
he always throw in

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:19.051
some weird parenthetical
"as usual"?

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:20.686
He talks about the media

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:23.188
like a sitcom wife complaining
about her idiot husband.

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:25.090
"Kevin's watching the game
with his buddies,

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.193
while I'm stuck
chasing the kids around

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:30.563
and making dinner, as usual."

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.398
♪♪

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.233
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:39.138
So, Trump says

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:41.540
the fake news is responsible
for the incorrect statement

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:44.376
that he was willing to meet with
Iran without any preconditions.

00:05:44.376 --> 00:05:45.745
Man, I wonder
where the fake news

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:47.613
could have gotten
such a crazy idea.

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:49.181
-Secretary of State
Mike Pompeo says

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:52.785
the U.S. is ready to talk
to Iran with no preconditions.

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:54.653
-We're prepared to engage
in a conversation

00:05:54.653 --> 00:05:55.922
with no preconditions.

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:57.423
-Now, the president
has made clear,

00:05:57.423 --> 00:06:00.493
he's happy to take a meeting
with no preconditions.

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:01.994
-Secretary Pompeo,
for clarity on this,

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:04.630
can you foresee a meeting
between President Trump

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.465
and the Iranian leader
later this month

00:06:06.465 --> 00:06:08.801
surrounding the United Nations?
-Sure.

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:10.135
-Would the president
support that,

00:06:10.135 --> 00:06:11.303
and do you support that
actively?

00:06:11.303 --> 00:06:12.638
-The president's
made very clear,

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:14.807
he's prepared to meet
with no preconditions.

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:16.074
-Oh, my God.

00:06:16.074 --> 00:06:18.978
The fake news is coming
from inside the house.

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.012
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.580
As usual.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:23.749
♪♪

00:06:23.749 --> 00:06:27.519
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:27.519 --> 00:06:29.221
-Who knows? Who knows?

00:06:29.221 --> 00:06:31.290
Guys, you guys, who knows?

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.792
Maybe these Cabinet Secretaries
over here spreading fake news

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:34.994
are just misinformed.

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:36.762
I mean, it's not like
the president himself

00:06:36.762 --> 00:06:38.330
has ever said on TV
multiple times

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:41.300
that he would meet with Iran
with pre--

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.001
You know what?
Just roll the clips.

00:06:43.001 --> 00:06:44.870
-Do you have preconditions
for that meeting?

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:46.138
-No preconditions, no.

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:48.974
They want to meet, I'll meet.
Anytime they want.

00:06:48.974 --> 00:06:51.343
Anytime they want.
It's good for the country,

00:06:51.343 --> 00:06:54.980
good for them, good for us,
and good for the world.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.382
No preconditions.

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:59.051
You want to talk good. Otherwise
you can have a bad economy

00:06:59.051 --> 00:07:00.853
for the next four years.
-No preconditions?

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:03.555
-Not as far as I'm concerned,
no preconditions.

00:07:03.555 --> 00:07:05.224
-Chuck Todd goes out of his way

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:07.826
to lock Trump into his comment
of no preconditions.

00:07:07.826 --> 00:07:10.996
It's as if he knows Trump is
a week away from him denying it.

00:07:10.996 --> 00:07:12.664
"And you're not going
to leave this interview

00:07:12.664 --> 00:07:14.300
and immediately say
this is fake news?"

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.001
[ As Trump ] Absolutely not.

00:07:16.001 --> 00:07:17.970
[ Normal voice ]
"Because I see you have
Twitter open on your phone.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.972
You're not tweeting that right
now, are you?

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:24.977
[ As Trump ] Absolutely not.
How many K's in the word "fake"?

00:07:24.977 --> 00:07:28.781
[ Normal voice ]
The reason Trump keeps waffling
between confrontation with Iran

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.950
and deal-making with Iran
is pretty simple.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.618
He doesn't know anything
about any of this.

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:35.888
He has no actual world view, and
he doesn't know what he wants.

00:07:35.888 --> 00:07:38.090
Sometimes, he claims to be
against Middle East wars.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:39.558
Other times, he takes orders

00:07:39.558 --> 00:07:42.161
from the dictators he's friendly
with, like in this case,

00:07:42.161 --> 00:07:44.763
Saudi Arabia's Crown Prince
Mohammad Bin Salman.

00:07:44.763 --> 00:07:46.098
Trump is so close to MBS

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:48.901
and so proud of our arms sales
to Saudi Arabia

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.602
that when they met last year
in the Oval Office,

00:07:50.602 --> 00:07:53.038
Trump literally showed off
giant posters

00:07:53.038 --> 00:07:55.440
of the weapons
he was selling to the Kingdom.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:56.709
-We've become very good friends

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:59.311
over a fairly short
period of time.

00:07:59.311 --> 00:08:03.749
I was in Saudi Arabia in May,
and we are bringing back

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:06.719
hundreds of billions of dollars
into the United States.

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:10.422
If you look,
in terms of dollars,

00:08:10.422 --> 00:08:15.260
$3 billion, $533 million.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:18.431
$525 million.

00:08:18.431 --> 00:08:22.634
$6 billion, that's for frigates.

00:08:22.634 --> 00:08:25.737
$889 million, $63 million.

00:08:25.737 --> 00:08:30.676
THAAD system, $13 billion.

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:33.912
The C-130 heli-- airplanes,

00:08:33.912 --> 00:08:36.548
the Hercules, great plane,

00:08:36.548 --> 00:08:39.151
$3.8 billion.

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:41.186
The Bradley Vehicles,

00:08:41.186 --> 00:08:44.256
that's the tanks, $1.2 billion.

00:08:44.256 --> 00:08:46.525
-He's selling billions
of dollars in weapons

00:08:46.525 --> 00:08:48.527
to a tyrannical regime,
and he's acting like

00:08:48.527 --> 00:08:50.963
he's showing him the menu
at a restaurant.

00:08:50.963 --> 00:08:52.765
[ As Trump ]
And if you look over here,

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:54.032
you'll see tonight's special.

00:08:54.032 --> 00:08:57.703
We got the Bradley tanks.
Those are fresh.

00:08:57.703 --> 00:09:00.606
They just came in. The Hercules
airplanes, two for one.

00:09:00.606 --> 00:09:02.875
And of course,
our house specialty,

00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:06.879
the pommes frigates.

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:10.015
Do you want some pommes frigates
for the table?

00:09:10.015 --> 00:09:11.884
To share while you wait?

00:09:11.884 --> 00:09:13.319
[ Applause ]

00:09:13.319 --> 00:09:16.255
[ Normal voice ] Now, the reason
Trump is suddenly backpedaling

00:09:16.255 --> 00:09:17.456
on his outreach to Iran

00:09:17.456 --> 00:09:19.525
is that Saudi Arabia
and Iran are rivals

00:09:19.525 --> 00:09:21.860
who are engaged
in a bunch of proxy wars,

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:24.596
and Saudi Arabia wants America's
help in that conflict.

00:09:24.596 --> 00:09:26.298
So last night, Trump threatened

00:09:26.298 --> 00:09:29.301
an illegal and unconstitutional
war with Iran

00:09:29.301 --> 00:09:31.103
on, where else, Twitter.

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:33.639
-"Saudi Arabia oil supply
was attacked.

00:09:33.639 --> 00:09:36.342
There is reason to believe
that we know the culprit,

00:09:36.342 --> 00:09:39.245
are locked and loaded
depending on verification,

00:09:39.245 --> 00:09:40.745
but are waiting to hear
from the Kingdom

00:09:40.745 --> 00:09:43.682
as to who they believe
was the cause of this attack,

00:09:43.682 --> 00:09:46.686
and under what terms
we would proceed!"

00:09:46.686 --> 00:09:48.120
-Think about how insane this is.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.721
The President
of the United States,

00:09:49.721 --> 00:09:51.256
the guy who spent
the entire campaign

00:09:51.256 --> 00:09:54.093
falsely claiming he wanted
to stay out of the Middle East

00:09:54.093 --> 00:09:55.261
and would put America first

00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:57.296
just threatened a war with Iran
on Twitter

00:09:57.296 --> 00:09:58.497
and said he was waiting

00:09:58.497 --> 00:10:00.399
for Saudi Arabia
to tell him what to do.

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:02.100
I never thought I'd say this,
but someone needs

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:05.470
to let American Pharoah loose
in the Oval Office.

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:06.805
He doesn't even need
to bite Trump.

00:10:06.805 --> 00:10:08.407
Just chase him around
for a while.

00:10:08.407 --> 00:10:10.409
Keep him distracted.

00:10:10.409 --> 00:10:11.743
[ As Trump ] Mike Pence.

00:10:11.743 --> 00:10:13.778
Mike Pence is the one you want.

00:10:13.778 --> 00:10:15.948
Pence ratted you out!

00:10:15.948 --> 00:10:17.616
[ Normal voice ]
And let's not forget.

00:10:17.616 --> 00:10:19.451
Let's not forget,
we also have no idea

00:10:19.451 --> 00:10:21.687
what Trump's personal
financial motivations are here

00:10:21.687 --> 00:10:23.122
when it comes to Saudi Arabia.

00:10:23.122 --> 00:10:26.959
So far, all we do know is that
Trump registered eight companies

00:10:26.959 --> 00:10:29.462
in Saudi Arabia
during the 2016 campaign.

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:33.298
Saudi lobbyists spent $270,000
at Trump's hotel

00:10:33.298 --> 00:10:35.101
in December 2016.

00:10:35.101 --> 00:10:37.636
A visit from Saudi officials
to Trump's international hotel

00:10:37.636 --> 00:10:40.038
in New York City helped boost
the hotel's quarterly revenue

00:10:40.038 --> 00:10:42.741
by 13% in 2018's first quarter.

00:10:42.741 --> 00:10:45.644
And on top of all that,
he and the King of Saudi Arabia

00:10:45.644 --> 00:10:50.716
touched that weird, glowing orb
during a trip to Riyadh in 2017,

00:10:50.716 --> 00:10:54.553
where it's possible
they Freaky-Friday'd.

00:10:54.553 --> 00:10:56.222
Now, look. look.

00:10:56.222 --> 00:10:58.023
It is always hard,

00:10:58.023 --> 00:11:00.159
almost impossible
to prove body-swapping,

00:11:00.159 --> 00:11:03.262
but think of how well Donald
Trump has treated Saudi Arabia

00:11:03.262 --> 00:11:05.030
post-orb.

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:06.732
Of course, if the King
is in Trump's body,

00:11:06.732 --> 00:11:09.501
then that means Trump
is inside the King's body.

00:11:09.501 --> 00:11:11.804
Has anyone checked in
on the King?

00:11:11.804 --> 00:11:13.139
[Bleep]

00:11:13.139 --> 00:11:16.308
[ Laughter ]

00:11:16.308 --> 00:11:17.576
And now that Democrats
in Congress

00:11:17.576 --> 00:11:19.344
are investigating
Trump's financial conflicts,

00:11:19.344 --> 00:11:21.213
Trump is lashing out
and calling on Congress

00:11:21.213 --> 00:11:24.616
to investigate former President
Obama for a deal Obama made

00:11:24.616 --> 00:11:27.820
to produce content for Netflix
after his presidency was over,

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:30.956
although, again, Trump's Twitter
syntax was hard to follow.

00:11:30.956 --> 00:11:32.992
Trump wrote, "They failed
on the Mueller Report,

00:11:32.992 --> 00:11:34.726
they failed on
Robert Mueller's testimony,

00:11:34.726 --> 00:11:36.261
they failed on everything else,

00:11:36.261 --> 00:11:38.497
so now the Democrats
are trying to build a case

00:11:38.497 --> 00:11:40.699
that I enrich myself
by being President.

00:11:40.699 --> 00:11:42.867
These Radical Left Democrats
are CRAZY!

00:11:42.867 --> 00:11:44.803
Obama Netflix?"

00:11:44.803 --> 00:11:48.040
[ Laughter ]

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.675
[ Laughing ]
Why does he say it like --

00:11:49.675 --> 00:11:53.812
Like, even he isn't sure
what he's saying makes sense.

00:11:53.812 --> 00:11:55.480
It's like if you get super high
with your buddies

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.349
and try to decide
what to put on TV

00:11:57.349 --> 00:11:59.985
but you can't really get
the words out of your mouth?

00:11:59.985 --> 00:12:01.620
"Dude, what should we watch?"

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:04.889
[ Imitating bong bubbling ]

00:12:04.889 --> 00:12:07.826
"Obama Netflix?

00:12:07.826 --> 00:12:09.795
Is that it?

00:12:09.795 --> 00:12:11.864
Is that it?"
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:15.167 --> 00:12:17.302
If anything, it sounds like
a new slang term

00:12:17.302 --> 00:12:19.538
for when you want to invite
a date over to your place

00:12:19.538 --> 00:12:22.908
but only to talk about
detailed policy proposals.

00:12:22.908 --> 00:12:24.976
"Hey, I got some ideas
for solving climate change.

00:12:24.976 --> 00:12:27.213
You want to come over
and Obama Netflix and chill?"

00:12:27.213 --> 00:12:28.513
[ Laughter ]

00:12:28.513 --> 00:12:30.916
This is why we can't take
anything Trump and his aides say

00:12:30.916 --> 00:12:33.285
at face value. They lie
about the smallest things,

00:12:33.285 --> 00:12:35.286
like horses,
to the biggest things, like war.

00:12:35.286 --> 00:12:37.522
They constantly contradict
themselves and each other,

00:12:37.522 --> 00:12:40.559
and we have no idea what their
hidden financial interests are.

00:12:40.559 --> 00:12:43.562
They lie and enrich themselves
while the rest of us run around

00:12:43.562 --> 00:12:45.798
and try to hold them
accountable.

00:12:45.798 --> 00:12:47.166
As usual.

00:12:47.166 --> 00:12:49.635
♪♪

00:12:49.635 --> 00:12:52.604
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:52.604 --> 00:12:54.273
This has been "A Closer Look."

